&lt;p&gt;We had someone who wired a doorbell camera to Twilio, hooked into the wrong event, and got roughly 500 texts in a minute. Someone who shipped a migration that also updated every user record and locked the database in production. Someone who kicked off a set of nested loops to brute force a hash, did the math, and worked out that it would finish in the year 2598.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smash Stories is that thread, except this time there are prizes!!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Need a bug? We got you.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clear the Lineup works with any existing codebase, and if you don't have your own project on hand, ours is open source. Forem powers DEV, and our &lt;a href="https://github.com/forem/forem/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aopen%20label%3Abug" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;open issues labeled &lt;code&gt;bug&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are sitting right there waiting for someone with an afternoon and a stubborn streak.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fair warning: new features, typos, and documentation fixes don't count for this one. We want the true bug fixes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Your odds are good right now
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We're a couple of weeks in and submissions are coming in at a steady trickle. All I’ll say is we have 20+ winners across five prize categories. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Category winners get drawn from a smaller pool than the overall pool, so &lt;strong&gt;Best Use of Sentry&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Best Use of Google AI&lt;/strong&gt; offer the best chances at winning. Sentry winners also get a super cool limited-edition skateboard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want a head start on the Sentry category, the Sentry team is doing a &lt;a href="https://dev.to/sentry/chasing-the-sentry-prize-for-devs-summer-bug-smash-let-us-know-what-questions-you-have-1506"&gt;live demo and Q&amp;amp;A&lt;/a&gt; on DEV this Thursday, July 30 at 11am PT / 2pm ET. Post your questions on the article to have them answered live!&lt;/p&gt;


